  "question": "Can an App enable auto-merge and enter the merge queue, and take a pull request out of it before the queue merges it? And does the poller read a change before the queue merges it? Does a push take a queued pull request out, can the queue eject one without merging it, its approval staying, is a draft ever merged by a person or the queue, and does the queue run the required checks on the merge group? Is each enqueue and dequeue on the pull request's timeline, naming its actor?",
  "pass": "Written 2026-11-13T12:29:00Z, before anything is read (issue 807's second box): read-only, as the Maintainer, of canary pull requests 58 (P-2.queue's C, ejected), 100 (P-2.no-pass's, queued by a person and merged) and 70 (P-2.queue-app's, queued by the queue App and merged): the timeline port's own read, `adapters/timeline.py` `events`, the REST timeline at per_page 100, of each; its read of 58's reviews, `reviews`, at per_page 100, with the repo's permission read of each login it asks and the compare of each review's commit against main's head, read once first; and the facts port's own query, `adapters/checks.py` QUERY, of 100 and 70. Each answer kept whole. Pass if all hold: (1) 58's timeline, whole, holds removed_from_merge_queue after added_to_merge_queue, by the merge queue's Bot, and no merged event, and its reviews, whole, hold the machine user's approval, approved, dismissed by no one; (2) 100's and 70's timelines, whole, each hold added_to_merge_queue, then merged, with no act between them by any account but the merge queue's, and each head's required check, p2-queue-check, reads concluded success through `adapters/checks.read`, whole. Fail if a port refuses a read, or any of these does not hold, naming which.",
